            <ArticleTitle>Buprenorphine in postoperative pain: results in 7500 patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>382-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Buprenorphine, a partial opiate-receptor agonist with potent analgesic properties, was given to 7548 patients in the immediate postoperative period. Ninety per cent of patients had good or adequate pain relief for at least 4 hours; there were few adverse effects and the incidence of drug-associated respiratory depression was estimated at less than 1%. There were no other side-effects of clinical note.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
